IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `gdpr-core`
IMPORT `gdpr-definitions`
IMPORT `P1-art-2`
IMPORT `P1-art-5`
IMPORT `P1-art-6`
IMPORT `P1-art-6b`
IMPORT `P1-art-7`
IMPORT `P1-art-8`
IMPORT `P1-art-9`
IMPORT `P1-art-10`
IMPORT `P1-art-11`
IMPORT `P1-art-24`

-- ============================================================================
-- P1-seat-controller.l4 -- THE SEAT LAYER OF P1: A CONTROLLER.  Articles 2, 4 (points 1, 2, 6, 7, 8), 5 to 11 and 24.
-- Written by P1 (Sonnet 5.5).  Every question calls a layer-1 rule and restates none.
--
-- SEAT: a controller: the body that, alone or jointly with others, determines the purposes and means of processing personal data (Art 4(7)); joint controllers are the same seat, with the plain input `decides them jointly with another body`.
-- Questions are phrased `Under Article N, as a controller, ...`, grouped under § headings in the text's order.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS.  Each input is a yes or no, a number, a date or a choice from a list, with an @desc.  Where a layer-1 rule takes a list or a MAYBE, the
-- list or MAYBE is built here from those plain answers (see the helpers below).  "Not sure" is offered only where a layer-1 rule combines several
-- answers (Article 6(1), 9(2)); it becomes NOTHING and the combining rule answers NOTHING unless another answer already decides it.
-- Borrowed facts (consent, child, necessity, "lawfully", "fairly") are asked as plain facts: PLAN.md section 6.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Regulation itself gives in its own words (a definition that "means", an "only if", a flat
-- "shall not", a "where"); NOTHING means the text does not answer on these facts.  Never read NOTHING as no (NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING").
-- A `Duty outcome` answers "the duty does not arise" (a failed gate), "the duty arises and is met" or "the duty arises and is not met".
--
-- THERE IS NO SEAT FOR AN OFFICIAL.  Where a provision addresses only an official or a lawmaker (Art 6(2), 6(3), 8(1) second subparagraph, 9(4)), the question asks what it means to the controller.
-- ============================================================================

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Helpers that build the layer-1 inputs from the plain answers.  They only translate; they restate no rule.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- A yes, a no, or "I am not sure", which becomes NOTHING.
DECLARE `P1 controller answer` IS ONE OF
    `P1 controller answer: yes`
    `P1 controller answer: no`
    `P1 controller answer: not sure`

GIVEN answer IS A `P1 controller answer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`P1 controller answer as a yes or no` MEANS
    CONSIDER answer
    WHEN `P1 controller answer: yes` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `P1 controller answer: no` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `P1 controller answer: not sure` THEN NOTHING

GIVEN `the person can be identified` IS A BOOLEAN
      means IS AN `Art 4(1) means of identification`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Art 4(1) means of identification`
`P1 controller ways of identification` MEANS
    IF `the person can be identified` THEN LIST means ELSE EMPTY

GIVEN `a Member State has provided an age` IS A BOOLEAN
      age IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`P1 controller age a Member State has provided` MEANS
    IF `a Member State has provided an age` THEN JUST age ELSE NOTHING

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A BOOLEAN
      d IS A BOOLEAN
      e IS A BOOLEAN
      f IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `Art 5 principle`
`P1 controller principles shown` MEANS
    (append (IF a THEN LIST `Art 5(1)(a) lawfulness, fairness and transparency` ELSE EMPTY) (append (IF b THEN LIST `Art 5(1)(b) purpose limitation` ELSE EMPTY) (append (IF c THEN LIST `Art 5(1)(c) data minimisation` ELSE EMPTY) (append (IF d THEN LIST `Art 5(1)(d) accuracy` ELSE EMPTY) (append (IF e THEN LIST `Art 5(1)(e) storage limitation` ELSE EMPTY) (IF f THEN LIST `Art 5(1)(f) integrity and confidentiality` ELSE EMPTY))))))

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A BOOLEAN
      d IS A BOOLEAN
      e IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `Art 6(4) matter to be taken into account`
`P1 controller matters of Art 6(4) shown` MEANS
    (append (IF a THEN LIST `Art 6(4)(a) any link between the purposes` ELSE EMPTY) (append (IF b THEN LIST `Art 6(4)(b) the context in which the personal data have been collected` ELSE EMPTY) (append (IF c THEN LIST `Art 6(4)(c) the nature of the personal data` ELSE EMPTY) (append (IF d THEN LIST `Art 6(4)(d) the possible consequences of the intended further processing for data subjects` ELSE EMPTY) (IF e THEN LIST `Art 6(4)(e) the existence of appropriate safeguards` ELSE EMPTY)))))

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A BOOLEAN
      d IS A BOOLEAN
      e IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `Art 24(1) matter taken into account`
`P1 controller matters of Art 24(1) shown` MEANS
    (append (IF a THEN LIST `Art 24(1) the nature of the processing` ELSE EMPTY) (append (IF b THEN LIST `Art 24(1) the scope of the processing` ELSE EMPTY) (append (IF c THEN LIST `Art 24(1) the context of the processing` ELSE EMPTY) (append (IF d THEN LIST `Art 24(1) the purposes of the processing` ELSE EMPTY) (IF e THEN LIST `Art 24(1) the risks of varying likelihood and severity for the rights and freedoms of natural persons` ELSE EMPTY)))))

§ `Regulation (EU) 2016/679, Articles 2 to 11 and 24 -- my questions as a controller`


§§ `Article 2 -- does the Regulation reach the processing?`

@export Under Article 2(1) and (2), as a controller, is my processing of personal data within the material scope of this Regulation?
GIVEN `the operations are processing of personal data` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the operations are processing of personal data? Answer true or false.
      `the processing is wholly or partly by automated means` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the processing is wholly or partly by automated means? Answer true or false.
      `the personal data form part of a filing system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the personal data form part of a filing system? Answer true or false.
      `the personal data are intended to form part of a filing system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the personal data are intended to form part of a filing system? Answer true or false.
      `the processing is in the course of an activity which falls outside the scope of Union law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the processing is in the course of an activity which falls outside the scope of Union law? Answer true or false.
      `the processing is by a Member State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the processing is by a Member State? Answer true or false.
      `the Member State is carrying out activities which fall within the scope of Chapter 2 of Title V of the TEU` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the Member State is carrying out activities which fall within the scope of Chapter 2 of Title V of the TEU? Answer true or false.
      `the processing is by a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the processing is by a natural person? Answer true or false.
      `the natural person processes in the course of a purely personal or household activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the natural person processes in the course of a purely personal or household activity? Answer true or false.
      `the processing is by a competent authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the processing is by a competent authority? Answer true or false.
      `the purpose of the processing` IS A `Art 2(2)(d) purpose of the processing` @desc The purpose of the processing: choose exactly one of: Art 2(2)(d) prevention of criminal offences; Art 2(2)(d) investigation of criminal offences; Art 2(2)(d) detection of criminal offences; Art 2(2)(d) prosecution of criminal offences; Art 2(2)(d) execution of criminal penalties; Art 2(2)(d) safeguarding against threats to public security; Art 2(2)(d) prevention of threats to public security; Art 2(2)(d) another purpose.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 2(1) and (2), as a controller, is my processing of personal data within the material scope of this Regulation` IS
    `Art 2(1) and (2) the processing is within the material scope of this Regulation` (`Art 2(1) this Regulation applies to the processing of personal data` `the operations are processing of personal data` `the processing is wholly or partly by automated means` `the personal data form part of a filing system` `the personal data are intended to form part of a filing system`) (`Art 2(2) this Regulation applies to the processing of personal data, given points (a) to (d)` (`Art 2(2)(a) this Regulation applies to processing in the course of an activity outside the scope of Union law` `the processing is in the course of an activity which falls outside the scope of Union law`) (`Art 2(2)(b) this Regulation applies to processing by the Member States in activities within Chapter 2 of Title V of the TEU` `the processing is by a Member State` `the Member State is carrying out activities which fall within the scope of Chapter 2 of Title V of the TEU`) (`Art 2(2)(c) this Regulation applies to processing by a natural person in the course of a purely personal or household activity` `the processing is by a natural person` `the natural person processes in the course of a purely personal or household activity`) (`Art 2(2)(d) this Regulation applies to processing by competent authorities for the purposes of criminal justice and public security` `the processing is by a competent authority` `the purpose of the processing`))


§§ `Article 4 -- who and what the definitions pick out`

@export Under Article 4(1), as a controller, is the information I hold personal data?
GIVEN `the information relates to a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the information relates to a natural person? Answer true or false.
      `the natural person is identified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the natural person is identified? Answer true or false.
      `the natural person can be identified directly or indirectly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the natural person can be identified directly or indirectly? Answer true or false.
      `how the natural person can be identified` IS A `Art 4(1) means of identification` @desc How the natural person can be identified: choose exactly one of: Art 4(1) a name; Art 4(1) an identification number; Art 4(1) location data; Art 4(1) an online identifier; Art 4(1) a factor specific to the physical identity; Art 4(1) a factor specific to the physiological identity; Art 4(1) a factor specific to the genetic identity; Art 4(1) a factor specific to the mental identity; Art 4(1) a factor specific to the economic identity; Art 4(1) a factor specific to the cultural identity; Art 4(1) a factor specific to the social identity; Art 4(1) some other means of identification.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 4(1), as a controller, is the information I hold personal data` IS
    `Art 4(1) the information is personal data` `the information relates to a natural person` `the natural person is identified` (`P1 controller ways of identification` `the natural person can be identified directly or indirectly` `how the natural person can be identified`)

@export Under Article 4(2), as a controller, is what I do with personal data processing?
GIVEN `what is done with the personal data` IS A `Art 4(2) operation on personal data` @desc What is done with the personal data: choose exactly one of: Art 4(2) collection; Art 4(2) recording; Art 4(2) organisation; Art 4(2) structuring; Art 4(2) storage; Art 4(2) adaptation; Art 4(2) alteration; Art 4(2) retrieval; Art 4(2) consultation; Art 4(2) use; Art 4(2) disclosure by transmission; Art 4(2) dissemination; Art 4(2) otherwise making available; Art 4(2) alignment; Art 4(2) combination; Art 4(2) restriction; Art 4(2) erasure; Art 4(2) destruction; Art 4(2) some other operation.
      `the operations are performed on personal data` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the operations are performed on personal data? Answer true or false.
      `the operations are performed on sets of personal data` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the operations are performed on sets of personal data? Answer true or false.
      `the operations are performed by automated means` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the operations are performed by automated means? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 4(2), as a controller, is what I do with personal data processing` IS
    `Art 4(2) the operations are processing` (LIST `what is done with the personal data`) `the operations are performed on personal data` `the operations are performed on sets of personal data` `the operations are performed by automated means`

@export Under Article 4(6), as a controller, is my set of personal data a filing system?
GIVEN `the set is structured` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the set is structured? Answer true or false.
      `the set consists of personal data` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the set consists of personal data? Answer true or false.
      `the data are accessible according to specific criteria` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the data are accessible according to specific criteria? Answer true or false.
      `how the set is arranged` IS A `Art 4(6) arrangement of a set of personal data` @desc How the set is arranged: choose exactly one of: Art 4(6) centralised; Art 4(6) decentralised; Art 4(6) dispersed on a functional basis; Art 4(6) dispersed on a geographical basis; Art 4(6) arranged in some other way.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 4(6), as a controller, is my set of personal data a filing system` IS
    `Art 4(6) the set is a filing system` `the set is structured` `the set consists of personal data` `the data are accessible according to specific criteria` `how the set is arranged`

@export Under Article 4(7), as a controller, am I a controller of this processing?
GIVEN `the kind of body` IS A `Kind of person or body` @desc The kind of body: choose exactly one of: natural person; legal person; public authority; agency; other body; not a person or body.
      `the body decides the purposes of the processing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the body decides the purposes of the processing? Answer true or false.
      `the body decides the means of the processing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the body decides the means of the processing? Answer true or false.
      `Union or Member State law determines the purposes and means of the processing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that Union or Member State law determines the purposes and means of the processing? Answer true or false.
      `that law provides for the body as the controller, or sets criteria for nominating the controller that the body meets` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that that law provides for the body as the controller, or sets criteria for nominating the controller that the body meets? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 4(7), as a controller, am I a controller of this processing` IS
    `Art 4(7) the body is a controller` `the kind of body` `the body decides the purposes of the processing` `the body decides the means of the processing` `Union or Member State law determines the purposes and means of the processing` `that law provides for the body as the controller, or sets criteria for nominating the controller that the body meets`

@export Under Article 4(7), as a controller, do I decide the purposes and means alone or jointly with others?
GIVEN `the body decides the purposes of the processing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the body decides the purposes of the processing? Answer true or false.
      `the body decides the means of the processing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the body decides the means of the processing? Answer true or false.
      `the body decides them jointly with another body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the body decides them jointly with another body? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE `Art 4(7) how a controller determines the purposes and means`
DECIDE `Under Article 4(7), as a controller, do I decide the purposes and means alone or jointly with others` IS
    `Art 4(7) how the body determines the purposes and means` `the body decides the purposes of the processing` `the body decides the means of the processing` `the body decides them jointly with another body`

@export Under Article 4(8), as a controller, is the body that processes personal data for me a processor?
GIVEN `the kind of body` IS A `Kind of person or body` @desc The kind of body: choose exactly one of: natural person; legal person; public authority; agency; other body; not a person or body.
      `the body processes personal data` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the body processes personal data? Answer true or false.
      `the body processes it on behalf of the controller` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the body processes it on behalf of the controller? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 4(8), as a controller, is the body that processes personal data for me a processor` IS
    `Art 4(8) the body is a processor` `the kind of body` `the body processes personal data` `the body processes it on behalf of the controller`


§§ `Article 5 -- the principles the processing must meet`

@export Under Article 5(1)(a), as a controller, are the personal data I process processed lawfully, fairly and in a transparent manner?
GIVEN `the personal data are processed lawfully` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the personal data are processed lawfully? Answer true or false.
      `the personal data are processed fairly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the personal data are processed fairly? Answer true or false.
      `the personal data are processed in a transparent manner in relation to the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the personal data are processed in a transparent manner in relation to the data subject? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 5(1)(a), as a controller, are the personal data I process processed lawfully, fairly and in a transparent manner` IS
    `Art 5(1)(a) the personal data are processed lawfully, fairly and in a transparent manner in relation to the data subject` `the personal data are processed lawfully` `the personal data are processed fairly` `the personal data are processed in a transparent manner in relation to the data subject`

@export Under Article 5(1)(b), as a controller, are the personal data collected for specified, explicit and legitimate purposes and not further processed incompatibly?
GIVEN `the purposes for which the personal data are collected are specified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the purposes for which the personal data are collected are specified? Answer true or false.
      `the purposes for which the personal data are collected are explicit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the purposes for which the personal data are collected are explicit? Answer true or false.
      `the purposes for which the personal data are collected are legitimate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the purposes for which the personal data are collected are legitimate? Answer true or false.
      `the personal data are further processed in a manner that is incompatible with those purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the personal data are further processed in a manner that is incompatible with those purposes? Answer true or false.
      `the purpose of the further processing` IS A `Art 5(1)(b) purpose of archiving, research or statistics` @desc The purpose of the further processing: choose exactly one of: Art 5(1)(b) archiving purposes in the public interest; Art 5(1)(b) scientific research purposes; Art 5(1)(b) historical research purposes; Art 5(1)(b) statistical purposes; Art 5(1)(b) some other purpose.
      `the further processing is in accordance with Article 89(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the further processing is in accordance with Article 89(1)? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 5(1)(b), as a controller, are the personal data collected for specified, explicit and legitimate purposes and not further processed incompatibly` IS
    `Art 5(1)(b) the personal data are collected for specified, explicit and legitimate purposes and not further processed in a manner that is incompatible with those purposes` `the purposes for which the personal data are collected are specified` `the purposes for which the personal data are collected are explicit` `the purposes for which the personal data are collected are legitimate` `the personal data are further processed in a manner that is incompatible with those purposes` (`Art 5(1)(b) the further processing is considered incompatible with the initial purposes` `the purpose of the further processing` `the further processing is in accordance with Article 89(1)`)

@export Under Article 5(1)(c), as a controller, are the personal data I process adequate, relevant and limited to what is necessary?
GIVEN `the personal data are adequate in relation to the purposes for which they are processed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the personal data are adequate in relation to the purposes for which they are processed? Answer true or false.
      `the personal data are relevant in relation to the purposes for which they are processed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the personal data are relevant in relation to the purposes for which they are processed? Answer true or false.
      `the personal data are limited to what is necessary in relation to the purposes for which they are processed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the personal data are limited to what is necessary in relation to the purposes for which they are processed? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 5(1)(c), as a controller, are the personal data I process adequate, relevant and limited to what is necessary` IS
    `Art 5(1)(c) the personal data are adequate, relevant and limited to what is necessary in relation to the purposes for which they are processed` `the personal data are adequate in relation to the purposes for which they are processed` `the personal data are relevant in relation to the purposes for which they are processed` `the personal data are limited to what is necessary in relation to the purposes for which they are processed`

@export Under Article 5(1)(d), as a controller, are the personal data I process accurate and, where necessary, kept up to date?
GIVEN `the personal data are accurate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the personal data are accurate? Answer true or false.
      `keeping the personal data up to date is necessary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that keeping the personal data up to date is necessary? Answer true or false.
      `the personal data are kept up to date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the personal data are kept up to date? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 5(1)(d), as a controller, are the personal data I process accurate and, where necessary, kept up to date` IS
    `Art 5(1)(d) the personal data are accurate and, where necessary, kept up to date` `the personal data are accurate` `keeping the personal data up to date is necessary` `the personal data are kept up to date`

@export Under Article 5(1)(d), as a controller, have I taken every reasonable step to erase or rectify inaccurate personal data without delay?
GIVEN `some of the personal data are inaccurate, having regard to the purposes for which they are processed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that some of the personal data are inaccurate, having regard to the purposes for which they are processed? Answer true or false.
      `every reasonable step has been taken to erase or rectify the inaccurate personal data without delay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that every reasonable step has been taken to erase or rectify the inaccurate personal data without delay? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE `Duty outcome`
DECIDE `Under Article 5(1)(d), as a controller, have I taken every reasonable step to erase or rectify inaccurate personal data without delay` IS
    `Art 5(1)(d) every reasonable step is taken to ensure that inaccurate personal data are erased or rectified without delay` `some of the personal data are inaccurate, having regard to the purposes for which they are processed` `every reasonable step has been taken to erase or rectify the inaccurate personal data without delay`

@export Under Article 5(1)(e), as a controller, do I keep the personal data in a form which permits identification no longer than is necessary?
GIVEN `the personal data are kept in a form which permits identification of data subjects` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the personal data are kept in a form which permits identification of data subjects? Answer true or false.
      `they are kept for longer than is necessary for the purposes for which they are processed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that they are kept for longer than is necessary for the purposes for which they are processed? Answer true or false.
      `the personal data will be processed solely for` IS A `Art 5(1)(b) purpose of archiving, research or statistics` @desc The personal data will be processed solely for: choose exactly one of: Art 5(1)(b) archiving purposes in the public interest; Art 5(1)(b) scientific research purposes; Art 5(1)(b) historical research purposes; Art 5(1)(b) statistical purposes; Art 5(1)(b) some other purpose.
      `the processing is in accordance with Article 89(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the processing is in accordance with Article 89(1)? Answer true or false.
      `the appropriate technical and organisational measures required by this Regulation are implemented to safeguard the rights and freedoms of the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the appropriate technical and organisational measures required by this Regulation are implemented to safeguard the rights and freedoms of the data subject? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 5(1)(e), as a controller, do I keep the personal data in a form which permits identification no longer than is necessary` IS
    `Art 5(1)(e) the personal data are kept in a form which permits identification of data subjects for no longer than is necessary for the purposes for which they are processed` `the personal data are kept in a form which permits identification of data subjects` `they are kept for longer than is necessary for the purposes for which they are processed` (`Art 5(1)(e) the personal data may be stored for longer periods` `the personal data will be processed solely for` `the processing is in accordance with Article 89(1)` `the appropriate technical and organisational measures required by this Regulation are implemented to safeguard the rights and freedoms of the data subject`)

@export Under Article 5(1)(f), as a controller, are the personal data processed in a manner that ensures appropriate security?
GIVEN `the personal data are protected against unauthorised or unlawful processing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the personal data are protected against unauthorised or unlawful processing? Answer true or false.
      `the personal data are protected against accidental loss, destruction or damage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the personal data are protected against accidental loss, destruction or damage? Answer true or false.
      `appropriate technical or organisational measures are used` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that appropriate technical or organisational measures are used? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 5(1)(f), as a controller, are the personal data processed in a manner that ensures appropriate security` IS
    `Art 5(1)(f) the personal data are processed in a manner that ensures appropriate security, using appropriate technical or organisational measures` `the personal data are protected against unauthorised or unlawful processing` `the personal data are protected against accidental loss, destruction or damage` `appropriate technical or organisational measures are used`

@export Under Article 5(2), as a controller, am I responsible for compliance with Article 5(1)?
GIVEN `I am the controller` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that I am the controller? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 5(2), as a controller, am I responsible for compliance with Article 5(1)` IS
    `Art 5(2) the body is responsible for compliance with Art 5(1)` `I am the controller`

@export Under Article 5(2), as a controller, am I able to demonstrate compliance with Article 5(1)?
GIVEN `I can demonstrate lawfulness, fairness and transparency (Art 5(1)(a))` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you demonstrate compliance with 5(1)(a? Answer true or false.
      `I can demonstrate purpose limitation (Art 5(1)(b))` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you demonstrate compliance with 5(1)(b? Answer true or false.
      `I can demonstrate data minimisation (Art 5(1)(c))` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you demonstrate compliance with 5(1)(c? Answer true or false.
      `I can demonstrate accuracy (Art 5(1)(d))` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you demonstrate compliance with 5(1)(d? Answer true or false.
      `I can demonstrate storage limitation (Art 5(1)(e))` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you demonstrate compliance with 5(1)(e? Answer true or false.
      `I can demonstrate integrity and confidentiality (Art 5(1)(f))` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you demonstrate compliance with 5(1)(f? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 5(2), as a controller, am I able to demonstrate compliance with Article 5(1)` IS
    `Art 5(2) the controller is able to demonstrate compliance with Art 5(1)` (`P1 controller principles shown` `I can demonstrate lawfulness, fairness and transparency (Art 5(1)(a))` `I can demonstrate purpose limitation (Art 5(1)(b))` `I can demonstrate data minimisation (Art 5(1)(c))` `I can demonstrate accuracy (Art 5(1)(d))` `I can demonstrate storage limitation (Art 5(1)(e))` `I can demonstrate integrity and confidentiality (Art 5(1)(f))`)


§§ `Article 6 -- a lawful basis for the processing`

@export Under Article 6(1)(a), as a controller, has the data subject consented to the processing for one or more specific purposes?
GIVEN `the data subject has given consent to the processing of his or her personal data` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the data subject has given consent to the processing of his or her personal data? Answer true or false.
      `the consent is for one or more specific purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the consent is for one or more specific purposes? Answer true or false.
      `the processing is for one of those purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the processing is for one of those purposes? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 6(1)(a), as a controller, has the data subject consented to the processing for one or more specific purposes` IS
    `Art 6(1)(a) point (a) applies: the data subject has given consent to the processing for one or more specific purposes` `the data subject has given consent to the processing of his or her personal data` `the consent is for one or more specific purposes` `the processing is for one of those purposes`

@export Under Article 6(1)(b), as a controller, is the processing necessary for a contract with the data subject or for steps before one?
GIVEN `the processing is necessary for the performance of a contract to which the data subject is party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the processing is necessary for the performance of a contract to which the data subject is party? Answer true or false.
      `the processing is necessary in order to take steps at the request of the data subject prior to entering into a contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the processing is necessary in order to take steps at the request of the data subject prior to entering into a contract? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 6(1)(b), as a controller, is the processing necessary for a contract with the data subject or for steps before one` IS
    `Art 6(1)(b) point (b) applies: the processing is necessary for a contract with the data subject or for steps before one` `the processing is necessary for the performance of a contract to which the data subject is party` `the processing is necessary in order to take steps at the request of the data subject prior to entering into a contract`

@export Under Article 6(1)(c), as a controller, is the processing necessary for compliance with a legal obligation to which I am subject?
GIVEN `the processing is necessary for compliance with a legal obligation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the processing is necessary for compliance with a legal obligation? Answer true or false.
      `the controller is subject to that legal obligation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the controller is subject to that legal obligation? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 6(1)(c), as a controller, is the processing necessary for compliance with a legal obligation to which I am subject` IS
    `Art 6(1)(c) point (c) applies: the processing is necessary for compliance with a legal obligation to which the controller is subject` `the processing is necessary for compliance with a legal obligation` `the controller is subject to that legal obligation`

@export Under Article 6(1)(d), as a controller, is the processing necessary to protect the vital interests of the data subject or of another natural person?
GIVEN `the processing is necessary in order to protect vital interests` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the processing is necessary in order to protect vital interests? Answer true or false.
      `whose vital interests` IS A `Art 6(1)(d) whose vital interests` @desc Whose vital interests: choose exactly one of: Art 6(1)(d) the data subject's; Art 6(1)(d) another natural person's; Art 6(1)(d) the interests of something that is not a natural person.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 6(1)(d), as a controller, is the processing necessary to protect the vital interests of the data subject or of another natural person` IS
    `Art 6(1)(d) point (d) applies: the processing is necessary in order to protect the vital interests of the data subject or of another natural person` `the processing is necessary in order to protect vital interests` `whose vital interests`

@export Under Article 6(1)(e), as a controller, is the processing necessary for a task in the public interest or in the exercise of official authority vested in me?
GIVEN `the processing is necessary for the performance of a task carried out in the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the processing is necessary for the performance of a task carried out in the public interest? Answer true or false.
      `the processing is necessary in the exercise of official authority vested in the controller` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the processing is necessary in the exercise of official authority vested in the controller? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 6(1)(e), as a controller, is the processing necessary for a task in the public interest or in the exercise of official authority vested in me` IS
    `Art 6(1)(e) point (e) applies: the processing is necessary for a task in the public interest or in the exercise of official authority vested in the controller` `the processing is necessary for the performance of a task carried out in the public interest` `the processing is necessary in the exercise of official authority vested in the controller`

@export Under Article 6(1)(f), as a controller, does point (f) (legitimate interests) apply to my processing?
GIVEN `the processing is necessary for the purposes of the legitimate interests pursued by the controller or by a third party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the processing is necessary for the purposes of the legitimate interests pursued by the controller or by a third party? Answer true or false.
      `those interests are overridden by the interests or fundamental rights and freedoms of the data subject which require protection of personal data` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that those interests are overridden by the interests or fundamental rights and freedoms of the data subject which require protection of personal data? Answer true or false.
      `the data subject is a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the data subject is a child? Answer true or false.
      `the processing is carried out by a public authority in the performance of its tasks` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the processing is carried out by a public authority in the performance of its tasks? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 6(1)(f), as a controller, does point (f) (legitimate interests) apply to my processing` IS
    `Art 6(1)(f) point (f) applies: the processing is necessary for legitimate interests that are not overridden` `the processing is necessary for the purposes of the legitimate interests pursued by the controller or by a third party` `those interests are overridden by the interests or fundamental rights and freedoms of the data subject which require protection of personal data` `the data subject is a child` `the processing is carried out by a public authority in the performance of its tasks`

@export Under Article 6(1), as a controller, is the condition met that at least one of points (a) to (f) applies to my processing?
GIVEN `point (a) applies: consent` IS A `P1 controller answer` @desc Does point (a) apply to your processing (the data subject gave consent for specific purposes)? Answer P1 controller answer: yes, P1 controller answer: no or P1 controller answer: not sure (not sure is treated as not covered).
      `point (b) applies: contract` IS A `P1 controller answer` @desc Does point (b) apply (necessary for a contract with the data subject or for steps before one)? Answer P1 controller answer: yes, P1 controller answer: no or P1 controller answer: not sure (not sure is treated as not covered).
      `point (c) applies: legal obligation` IS A `P1 controller answer` @desc Does point (c) apply (necessary for compliance with a legal obligation to which you are subject)? Answer P1 controller answer: yes, P1 controller answer: no or P1 controller answer: not sure (not sure is treated as not covered).
      `point (d) applies: vital interests` IS A `P1 controller answer` @desc Does point (d) apply (necessary to protect vital interests of the data subject or of another natural person)? Answer P1 controller answer: yes, P1 controller answer: no or P1 controller answer: not sure (not sure is treated as not covered).
      `point (e) applies: public interest or official authority` IS A `P1 controller answer` @desc Does point (e) apply (necessary for a task in the public interest or in the exercise of official authority vested in you)? Answer P1 controller answer: yes, P1 controller answer: no or P1 controller answer: not sure (not sure is treated as not covered).
      `point (f) applies: legitimate interests` IS A `P1 controller answer` @desc Does point (f) apply (necessary for legitimate interests, not overridden)? Answer P1 controller answer: yes, P1 controller answer: no or P1 controller answer: not sure (not sure is treated as not covered).
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 6(1), as a controller, is the condition met that at least one of points (a) to (f) applies to my processing` IS
    `Art 6(1) the condition is met that at least one of points (a) to (f) applies` (`P1 controller answer as a yes or no` `point (a) applies: consent`) (`P1 controller answer as a yes or no` `point (b) applies: contract`) (`P1 controller answer as a yes or no` `point (c) applies: legal obligation`) (`P1 controller answer as a yes or no` `point (d) applies: vital interests`) (`P1 controller answer as a yes or no` `point (e) applies: public interest or official authority`) (`P1 controller answer as a yes or no` `point (f) applies: legitimate interests`)

@export Under Article 6(2), as a controller, may a Member State maintain or introduce more specific provisions for my processing?
GIVEN `the basis of the processing` IS A `Art 6(1) lawful basis` @desc The basis of the processing: choose exactly one of: Art 6(1)(a) consent; Art 6(1)(b) contract; Art 6(1)(c) legal obligation; Art 6(1)(d) vital interests; Art 6(1)(e) public interest or official authority; Art 6(1)(f) legitimate interests.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 6(2), as a controller, may a Member State maintain or introduce more specific provisions for my processing` IS
    `Art 6(2) a Member State may maintain or introduce more specific provisions to adapt the application of this Regulation to the processing` `the basis of the processing`

@export Under Article 6(3), as a controller, is the basis for my processing laid down by Union law or by Member State law to which I am subject?
GIVEN `the basis of the processing` IS A `Art 6(1) lawful basis` @desc The basis of the processing: choose exactly one of: Art 6(1)(a) consent; Art 6(1)(b) contract; Art 6(1)(c) legal obligation; Art 6(1)(d) vital interests; Art 6(1)(e) public interest or official authority; Art 6(1)(f) legitimate interests.
      `the basis is laid down by Union law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the basis is laid down by Union law? Answer true or false.
      `the basis is laid down by Member State law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the basis is laid down by Member State law? Answer true or false.
      `the controller is subject to that Member State law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the controller is subject to that Member State law? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 6(3), as a controller, is the basis for my processing laid down by Union law or by Member State law to which I am subject` IS
    `Art 6(3) the basis for the processing is laid down by Union law or by Member State law to which the controller is subject` `the basis of the processing` `the basis is laid down by Union law` `the basis is laid down by Member State law` `the controller is subject to that Member State law`

@export Under Article 6(3), as a controller, is the purpose of my processing determined in the legal basis or, for point (e), necessary for the task?
GIVEN `the basis of the processing` IS A `Art 6(1) lawful basis` @desc The basis of the processing: choose exactly one of: Art 6(1)(a) consent; Art 6(1)(b) contract; Art 6(1)(c) legal obligation; Art 6(1)(d) vital interests; Art 6(1)(e) public interest or official authority; Art 6(1)(f) legitimate interests.
      `the purpose of the processing is determined in that legal basis` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the purpose of the processing is determined in that legal basis? Answer true or false.
      `the processing is necessary for the performance of a task carried out in the public interest or in the exercise of official authority vested in the controller` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the processing is necessary for the performance of a task carried out in the public interest or in the exercise of official authority vested in the controller? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 6(3), as a controller, is the purpose of my processing determined in the legal basis or, for point (e), necessary for the task` IS
    `Art 6(3) the purpose of the processing is determined in the legal basis or, for point (e), is necessary for the task` `the basis of the processing` `the purpose of the processing is determined in that legal basis` `the processing is necessary for the performance of a task carried out in the public interest or in the exercise of official authority vested in the controller`

@export Under Article 6(3), as a controller, may the legal basis for my processing contain specific provisions on this matter?
GIVEN `the matter the legal basis would adapt` IS A `Art 6(3) matter a legal basis may adapt` @desc The matter the legal basis would adapt: choose exactly one of: Art 6(3) the general conditions governing the lawfulness of processing by the controller; Art 6(3) the types of data which are subject to the processing; Art 6(3) the data subjects concerned; Art 6(3) the entities to which the personal data may be disclosed; Art 6(3) the purposes for which the personal data may be disclosed; Art 6(3) the purpose limitation; Art 6(3) storage periods; Art 6(3) processing operations and processing procedures, including measures to ensure lawful and fair processing; Art 6(3) some other matter.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 6(3), as a controller, may the legal basis for my processing contain specific provisions on this matter` IS
    `Art 6(3) the legal basis may contain specific provisions to adapt the application of the rules of this Regulation on the matter` `the matter the legal basis would adapt`

@export Under Article 6(3), as a controller, does the law that is my legal basis meet an objective of public interest and stay proportionate to the legitimate aim pursued?
GIVEN `the law meets an objective of public interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the law meets an objective of public interest? Answer true or false.
      `the law is proportionate to the legitimate aim pursued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the law is proportionate to the legitimate aim pursued? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 6(3), as a controller, does the law that is my legal basis meet an objective of public interest and stay proportionate to the legitimate aim pursued` IS
    `Art 6(3) the Union or Member State law meets an objective of public interest and is proportionate to the legitimate aim pursued` `the law meets an objective of public interest` `the law is proportionate to the legitimate aim pursued`

@export Under Article 6(4), as a controller, must I take into account the matters (a) to (e), and have I, before processing for another purpose?
GIVEN `the processing is for a purpose other than that for which the personal data have been collected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the processing is for a purpose other than that for which the personal data have been collected? Answer true or false.
      `the processing is based on the data subject's consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the processing is based on the data subject's consent? Answer true or false.
      `the processing is based on a Union or Member State law which constitutes a necessary and proportionate measure in a democratic society to safeguard the objectives referred to in Article 23(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the processing is based on a Union or Member State law which constitutes a necessary and proportionate measure in a democratic society to safeguard the objectives referred to in Article 23(1)? Answer true or false.
      `I took into account any link between the purposes (Art 6(4)(a))` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that I took into account any link between the purposes (Art 6(4)(a))? Answer true or false.
      `I took into account the context in which the personal data have been collected (Art 6(4)(b))` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that I took into account the context in which the personal data have been collected (Art 6(4)(b))? Answer true or false.
      `I took into account the nature of the personal data (Art 6(4)(c))` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that I took into account the nature of the personal data (Art 6(4)(c))? Answer true or false.
      `I took into account the possible consequences for data subjects (Art 6(4)(d))` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that I took into account the possible consequences for data subjects (Art 6(4)(d))? Answer true or false.
      `I took into account the existence of appropriate safeguards (Art 6(4)(e))` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that I took into account the existence of appropriate safeguards (Art 6(4)(e))? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE `Duty outcome`
DECIDE `Under Article 6(4), as a controller, must I take into account the matters (a) to (e), and have I, before processing for another purpose` IS
    `Art 6(4) the controller takes into account the matters (a) to (e) in ascertaining whether processing for another purpose is compatible` `the processing is for a purpose other than that for which the personal data have been collected` `the processing is based on the data subject's consent` `the processing is based on a Union or Member State law which constitutes a necessary and proportionate measure in a democratic society to safeguard the objectives referred to in Article 23(1)` (`P1 controller matters of Art 6(4) shown` `I took into account any link between the purposes (Art 6(4)(a))` `I took into account the context in which the personal data have been collected (Art 6(4)(b))` `I took into account the nature of the personal data (Art 6(4)(c))` `I took into account the possible consequences for data subjects (Art 6(4)(d))` `I took into account the existence of appropriate safeguards (Art 6(4)(e))`)


§§ `Article 7 -- consent`

@export Under Article 7(1), as a controller, am I able to demonstrate that the data subject has consented?
GIVEN `the processing is based on consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the processing is based on consent? Answer true or false.
      `the controller is able to demonstrate that the data subject has consented to processing of his or her personal data` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the controller is able to demonstrate that the data subject has consented to processing of his or her personal data? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE `Duty outcome`
DECIDE `Under Article 7(1), as a controller, am I able to demonstrate that the data subject has consented` IS
    `Art 7(1) the controller is able to demonstrate that the data subject has consented` `the processing is based on consent` `the controller is able to demonstrate that the data subject has consented to processing of his or her personal data`

@export Under Article 7(2), as a controller, is the request for consent presented clearly where consent is given in a written declaration that also concerns other matters?
GIVEN `consent is given in the context of a written declaration which also concerns other matters` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that consent is given in the context of a written declaration which also concerns other matters? Answer true or false.
      `the request for consent is presented in a manner which is clearly distinguishable from the other matters` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the request for consent is presented in a manner which is clearly distinguishable from the other matters? Answer true or false.
      `the request is in an intelligible and easily accessible form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the request is in an intelligible and easily accessible form? Answer true or false.
      `the request uses clear and plain language` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the request uses clear and plain language? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE `Duty outcome`
DECIDE `Under Article 7(2), as a controller, is the request for consent presented clearly where consent is given in a written declaration that also concerns other matters` IS
    `Art 7(2) the request for consent is presented clearly where consent is given in a written declaration that also concerns other matters` `consent is given in the context of a written declaration which also concerns other matters` `the request for consent is presented in a manner which is clearly distinguishable from the other matters` `the request is in an intelligible and easily accessible form` `the request uses clear and plain language`

@export Under Article 7(2), as a controller, is a part of the declaration that infringes this Regulation binding?
GIVEN `the part is part of such a declaration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the part is part of such a declaration? Answer true or false.
      `the part constitutes an infringement of this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the part constitutes an infringement of this Regulation? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 7(2), as a controller, is a part of the declaration that infringes this Regulation binding` IS
    `Art 7(2) the part of the declaration is binding` `the part is part of such a declaration` `the part constitutes an infringement of this Regulation`

@export Under Article 7(3), as a controller, may the data subject withdraw his or her consent at any time?
GIVEN `the data subject has given consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the data subject has given consent? Answer true or false.
      `the day on which consent was given` IS A DATE @desc On what date: the day on which consent was given?
      `the day on which the data subject withdraws it` IS A DATE @desc On what date: the day on which the data subject withdraws it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 7(3), as a controller, may the data subject withdraw his or her consent at any time` IS
    `Art 7(3) the data subject may withdraw his or her consent at any time` `the data subject has given consent` `the day on which consent was given` `the day on which the data subject withdraws it`

@export Under Article 7(3), as a controller, does the data subject's withdrawal of consent affect the lawfulness of my earlier processing?
GIVEN `the processing was based on consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the processing was based on consent? Answer true or false.
      `the processing took place before the withdrawal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the processing took place before the withdrawal? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 7(3), as a controller, does the data subject's withdrawal of consent affect the lawfulness of my earlier processing` IS
    `Art 7(3) the withdrawal of consent affects the lawfulness of the processing` `the processing was based on consent` `the processing took place before the withdrawal`

@export Under Article 7(3), as a controller, was the data subject informed of the right to withdraw consent before giving consent?
GIVEN `the data subject has given consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the data subject has given consent? Answer true or false.
      `the data subject was informed of the right to withdraw consent before giving consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the data subject was informed of the right to withdraw consent before giving consent? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 7(3), as a controller, was the data subject informed of the right to withdraw consent before giving consent` IS
    `Art 7(3) the data subject was informed of the right to withdraw consent prior to giving consent` `the data subject has given consent` `the data subject was informed of the right to withdraw consent before giving consent`

@export Under Article 7(3), as a controller, is it as easy for the data subject to withdraw consent as to give it?
GIVEN `withdrawing consent is as easy as giving consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that withdrawing consent is as easy as giving consent? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 7(3), as a controller, is it as easy for the data subject to withdraw consent as to give it` IS
    `Art 7(3) it is as easy to withdraw consent as to give it` `withdrawing consent is as easy as giving consent`

@export Under Article 7(4), as a controller, is the conditionality of my contract on consent a matter of which utmost account is taken in assessing whether consent is freely given?
GIVEN `consent is being assessed for whether it is freely given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that consent is being assessed for whether it is freely given? Answer true or false.
      `the performance of a contract, including the provision of a service, is conditional on consent to the processing of personal data` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the performance of a contract, including the provision of a service, is conditional on consent to the processing of personal data? Answer true or false.
      `that processing is necessary for the performance of that contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that that processing is necessary for the performance of that contract? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 7(4), as a controller, is the conditionality of my contract on consent a matter of which utmost account is taken in assessing whether consent is freely given` IS
    `Art 7(4) the conditionality of the contract on consent that is not necessary for it is a matter of which utmost account is taken` `consent is being assessed for whether it is freely given` `the performance of a contract, including the provision of a service, is conditional on consent to the processing of personal data` `that processing is necessary for the performance of that contract`


§§ `Article 8 -- a child's consent to information society services`

@export Under Article 8(1), as a controller, does the processing of the child's personal data meet the condition of Article 8(1)?
GIVEN `point (a) of Article 6(1) applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that point (a) of Article 6(1) applies? Answer true or false.
