      `the information society services are offered directly to a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the information society services are offered directly to a child? Answer true or false.
      `the age of the child in complete years` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the age of the child in complete years? Give a number.
      `a Member State has provided by law for a lower age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that a Member State has provided by law for a lower age? Answer true or false.
      `the lower age a Member State has provided by law` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the lower age a Member State has provided by law? Give a number.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 8(1), as a controller, is the consent of the holder of parental responsibility needed for my processing` IS
    `Art 8(1) the case is one in which the consent of the holder of parental responsibility is needed` `point (a) of Article 6(1) applies` `the information society services are offered directly to a child` `the age of the child in complete years` (`P1 controller age a Member State has provided` `a Member State has provided by law for a lower age` `the lower age a Member State has provided by law`)

@export Under Article 8(1), as a controller, from what age may a child consent in my Member State?
GIVEN `a Member State has provided by law for a lower age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that a Member State has provided by law for a lower age? Answer true or false.
      `the lower age a Member State has provided by law` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the lower age a Member State has provided by law? Give a number.
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Article 8(1), as a controller, from what age may a child consent in my Member State` IS
    `Art 8(1) the age from which the child may consent in this Member State` (`P1 controller age a Member State has provided` `a Member State has provided by law for a lower age` `the lower age a Member State has provided by law`)

@export Under Article 8(1), as a controller, may a Member State provide by law for this lower age?
GIVEN `the lower age` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the lower age? Give a number.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 8(1), as a controller, may a Member State provide by law for this lower age` IS
    `Art 8(1) a Member State may provide by law for the lower age` `the lower age`

@export Under Article 8(2), as a controller, must I make reasonable efforts to verify that consent is given or authorised, and have I?
GIVEN `point (a) of Article 6(1) applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that point (a) of Article 6(1) applies? Answer true or false.
      `the information society services are offered directly to a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the information society services are offered directly to a child? Answer true or false.
      `the age of the child in complete years` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the age of the child in complete years? Give a number.
      `a Member State has provided by law for a lower age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that a Member State has provided by law for a lower age? Answer true or false.
      `the lower age a Member State has provided by law` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the lower age a Member State has provided by law? Give a number.
      `the controller has made reasonable efforts to verify that consent is given or authorised by the holder of parental responsibility` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the controller has made reasonable efforts to verify that consent is given or authorised by the holder of parental responsibility? Answer true or false.
      `the controller took available technology into consideration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the controller took available technology into consideration? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE `Duty outcome`
DECIDE `Under Article 8(2), as a controller, must I make reasonable efforts to verify that consent is given or authorised, and have I` IS
    `Art 8(2) the controller makes reasonable efforts to verify that consent is given or authorised, taking available technology into consideration` (`Art 8(1) the case is one in which the consent of the holder of parental responsibility is needed` `point (a) of Article 6(1) applies` `the information society services are offered directly to a child` `the age of the child in complete years` (`P1 controller age a Member State has provided` `a Member State has provided by law for a lower age` `the lower age a Member State has provided by law`)) `the controller has made reasonable efforts to verify that consent is given or authorised by the holder of parental responsibility` `the controller took available technology into consideration`

@export Under Article 8(3), as a controller, does Article 8(1) affect a rule of the general contract law of a Member State?
GIVEN `the rule is part of the general contract law of a Member State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the rule is part of the general contract law of a Member State? Answer true or false.
      `what the rule concerns` IS A `Art 8(3) what the rule of contract law concerns` @desc What the rule concerns: choose exactly one of: Art 8(3) the validity of a contract in relation to a child; Art 8(3) the formation of a contract in relation to a child; Art 8(3) the effect of a contract in relation to a child; Art 8(3) another rule of general contract law.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 8(3), as a controller, does Article 8(1) affect a rule of the general contract law of a Member State` IS
    `Art 8(3) paragraph 1 affects the rule of the general contract law of a Member State` `the rule is part of the general contract law of a Member State` `what the rule concerns`


§§ `Article 9 -- special categories of personal data`

@export Under Article 9(1), as a controller, are the personal data I process of a category the Regulation names?
GIVEN `the category of the personal data` IS A `Art 9(1) category of personal data` @desc The category of the personal data: choose exactly one of: Art 9(1) data revealing racial or ethnic origin; Art 9(1) data revealing political opinions; Art 9(1) data revealing religious or philosophical beliefs; Art 9(1) data revealing trade union membership; Art 9(1) genetic data; Art 9(1) biometric data for the purpose of uniquely identifying a natural person; Art 9(1) data concerning health; Art 9(1) data concerning a natural person's sex life or sexual orientation; Art 9(1) biometric data not for the purpose of uniquely identifying a natural person; Art 9(1) other personal data.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 9(1), as a controller, are the personal data I process of a category the Regulation names` IS
    `Art 9(1) the categories processed include one that paragraph 1 names` (LIST `the category of the personal data`)

@export Under Article 9(2)(a), as a controller, does point (a) (explicit consent) apply to my processing?
GIVEN `the data subject has given explicit consent to the processing of those personal data` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the data subject has given explicit consent to the processing of those personal data? Answer true or false.
      `the consent is for one or more specified purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the consent is for one or more specified purposes? Answer true or false.
      `Union or Member State law provides that the prohibition referred to in paragraph 1 may not be lifted by the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that Union or Member State law provides that the prohibition referred to in paragraph 1 may not be lifted by the data subject? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 9(2)(a), as a controller, does point (a) (explicit consent) apply to my processing` IS
    `Art 9(2)(a) point (a) applies: the data subject has given explicit consent to the processing for one or more specified purposes` `the data subject has given explicit consent to the processing of those personal data` `the consent is for one or more specified purposes` `Union or Member State law provides that the prohibition referred to in paragraph 1 may not be lifted by the data subject`

@export Under Article 9(2)(b), as a controller, does point (b) (employment and social security and social protection law) apply to my processing?
GIVEN `the processing is necessary for carrying out the obligations and exercising specific rights of the controller or of the data subject in the field of employment and social security and social protection law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the processing is necessary for carrying out the obligations and exercising specific rights of the controller or of the data subject in the field of employment and social security and social protection law? Answer true or false.
      `it is authorised by Union or Member State law or a collective agreement pursuant to Member State law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that it is authorised by Union or Member State law or a collective agreement pursuant to Member State law? Answer true or false.
      `that law or agreement provides for appropriate safeguards for the fundamental rights and the interests of the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that that law or agreement provides for appropriate safeguards for the fundamental rights and the interests of the data subject? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 9(2)(b), as a controller, does point (b) (employment and social security and social protection law) apply to my processing` IS
    `Art 9(2)(b) point (b) applies: the processing is necessary for employment and social security and social protection law` `the processing is necessary for carrying out the obligations and exercising specific rights of the controller or of the data subject in the field of employment and social security and social protection law` `it is authorised by Union or Member State law or a collective agreement pursuant to Member State law` `that law or agreement provides for appropriate safeguards for the fundamental rights and the interests of the data subject`

@export Under Article 9(2)(c), as a controller, does point (c) (vital interests where the data subject cannot give consent) apply to my processing?
GIVEN `the processing is necessary to protect vital interests` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the processing is necessary to protect vital interests? Answer true or false.
      `whose vital interests` IS A `Art 6(1)(d) whose vital interests` @desc Whose vital interests: choose exactly one of: Art 6(1)(d) the data subject's; Art 6(1)(d) another natural person's; Art 6(1)(d) the interests of something that is not a natural person.
      `the data subject is physically or legally incapable of giving consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the data subject is physically or legally incapable of giving consent? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 9(2)(c), as a controller, does point (c) (vital interests where the data subject cannot give consent) apply to my processing` IS
    `Art 9(2)(c) point (c) applies: the processing is necessary to protect vital interests where the data subject cannot give consent` `the processing is necessary to protect vital interests` `whose vital interests` `the data subject is physically or legally incapable of giving consent`

@export Under Article 9(2)(d), as a controller, does point (d) (a not-for-profit body and its members) apply to my processing?
GIVEN `the processing is carried out in the course of its legitimate activities with appropriate safeguards` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the processing is carried out in the course of its legitimate activities with appropriate safeguards? Answer true or false.
      `the body is` IS A `Art 9(2)(d) kind of body` @desc The body is: choose exactly one of: Art 9(2)(d) a foundation; Art 9(2)(d) an association; Art 9(2)(d) another not-for-profit body; Art 9(2)(d) a body that is not a not-for-profit body.
      `the body has` IS A `Art 9(2)(d) aim of the body` @desc The body has: choose exactly one of: Art 9(2)(d) a political aim; Art 9(2)(d) a philosophical aim; Art 9(2)(d) a religious aim; Art 9(2)(d) a trade union aim; Art 9(2)(d) some other aim.
      `the processing relates solely to the members or to former members of the body or to persons who have regular contact with it in connection with its purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the processing relates solely to the members or to former members of the body or to persons who have regular contact with it in connection with its purposes? Answer true or false.
      `the personal data are disclosed outside that body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the personal data are disclosed outside that body? Answer true or false.
      `the data subjects have consented to that disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the data subjects have consented to that disclosure? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 9(2)(d), as a controller, does point (d) (a not-for-profit body and its members) apply to my processing` IS
    `Art 9(2)(d) point (d) applies: a foundation, association or other not-for-profit body processes data of its members and those in regular contact with it` `the processing is carried out in the course of its legitimate activities with appropriate safeguards` `the body is` `the body has` `the processing relates solely to the members or to former members of the body or to persons who have regular contact with it in connection with its purposes` `the personal data are disclosed outside that body` `the data subjects have consented to that disclosure`

@export Under Article 9(2)(e), as a controller, does point (e) (data manifestly made public by the data subject) apply to my processing?
GIVEN `the processing relates to personal data which have been made public by the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the processing relates to personal data which have been made public by the data subject? Answer true or false.
      `the data subject made them public manifestly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the data subject made them public manifestly? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 9(2)(e), as a controller, does point (e) (data manifestly made public by the data subject) apply to my processing` IS
    `Art 9(2)(e) point (e) applies: the processing relates to personal data which are manifestly made public by the data subject` `the processing relates to personal data which have been made public by the data subject` `the data subject made them public manifestly`

@export Under Article 9(2)(f), as a controller, does point (f) (legal claims or courts acting in their judicial capacity) apply to my processing?
GIVEN `the processing is necessary for the establishment, exercise or defence of legal claims` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the processing is necessary for the establishment, exercise or defence of legal claims? Answer true or false.
      `the processing is whenever courts are acting in their judicial capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the processing is whenever courts are acting in their judicial capacity? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 9(2)(f), as a controller, does point (f) (legal claims or courts acting in their judicial capacity) apply to my processing` IS
    `Art 9(2)(f) point (f) applies: the processing is necessary for legal claims or whenever courts are acting in their judicial capacity` `the processing is necessary for the establishment, exercise or defence of legal claims` `the processing is whenever courts are acting in their judicial capacity`

@export Under Article 9(2)(g), as a controller, does point (g) (substantial public interest) apply to my processing?
GIVEN `the processing is necessary for reasons of substantial public interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the processing is necessary for reasons of substantial public interest? Answer true or false.
      `it is on the basis of Union or Member State law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that it is on the basis of Union or Member State law? Answer true or false.
      `that law is proportionate to the aim pursued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that that law is proportionate to the aim pursued? Answer true or false.
      `that law respects the essence of the right to data protection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that that law respects the essence of the right to data protection? Answer true or false.
      `that law provides for suitable and specific measures to safeguard the fundamental rights and the interests of the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that that law provides for suitable and specific measures to safeguard the fundamental rights and the interests of the data subject? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 9(2)(g), as a controller, does point (g) (substantial public interest) apply to my processing` IS
    `Art 9(2)(g) point (g) applies: the processing is necessary for reasons of substantial public interest on the basis of proportionate law` `the processing is necessary for reasons of substantial public interest` `it is on the basis of Union or Member State law` `that law is proportionate to the aim pursued` `that law respects the essence of the right to data protection` `that law provides for suitable and specific measures to safeguard the fundamental rights and the interests of the data subject`

@export Under Article 9(2)(h), as a controller, does point (h) (health or social care) apply to my processing?
GIVEN `the purpose of the processing` IS A `Art 9(2)(h) purpose` @desc The purpose of the processing: choose exactly one of: Art 9(2)(h) preventive medicine; Art 9(2)(h) occupational medicine; Art 9(2)(h) the assessment of the working capacity of the employee; Art 9(2)(h) medical diagnosis; Art 9(2)(h) the provision of health or social care or treatment; Art 9(2)(h) the management of health or social care systems and services; Art 9(2)(h) some other purpose.
      `the processing is necessary for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the processing is necessary for that purpose? Answer true or false.
      `the processing is on the basis of` IS A `Art 9(2)(h) basis` @desc The processing is on the basis of: choose exactly one of: Art 9(2)(h) Union law; Art 9(2)(h) Member State law; Art 9(2)(h) a contract with a health professional; Art 9(2)(h) none of these.
      `the conditions and safeguards referred to in paragraph 3 are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the conditions and safeguards referred to in paragraph 3 are met? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 9(2)(h), as a controller, does point (h) (health or social care) apply to my processing` IS
    `Art 9(2)(h) point (h) applies: the processing is necessary for preventive or occupational medicine, health or social care or treatment, or the management of health or social care systems` `the purpose of the processing` `the processing is necessary for that purpose` `the processing is on the basis of` `the conditions and safeguards referred to in paragraph 3 are met`

@export Under Article 9(2)(i), as a controller, does point (i) (public interest in the area of public health) apply to my processing?
GIVEN `the reason` IS A `Art 9(2)(i) reason` @desc The reason: choose exactly one of: Art 9(2)(i) protecting against serious cross-border threats to health; Art 9(2)(i) ensuring high standards of quality and safety of health care and of medicinal products or medical devices; Art 9(2)(i) another reason of public interest in the area of public health; Art 9(2)(i) no reason of public interest in the area of public health.
      `the processing is necessary for that reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the processing is necessary for that reason? Answer true or false.
      `it is on the basis of Union or Member State law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that it is on the basis of Union or Member State law? Answer true or false.
      `that law provides for suitable and specific measures to safeguard the rights and freedoms of the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that that law provides for suitable and specific measures to safeguard the rights and freedoms of the data subject? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 9(2)(i), as a controller, does point (i) (public interest in the area of public health) apply to my processing` IS
    `Art 9(2)(i) point (i) applies: the processing is necessary for reasons of public interest in the area of public health on the basis of law with suitable measures` `the reason` `the processing is necessary for that reason` `it is on the basis of Union or Member State law` `that law provides for suitable and specific measures to safeguard the rights and freedoms of the data subject`

@export Under Article 9(2)(j), as a controller, does point (j) (archiving, research or statistical purposes) apply to my processing?
GIVEN `the purpose` IS A `Art 5(1)(b) purpose of archiving, research or statistics` @desc The purpose: choose exactly one of: Art 5(1)(b) archiving purposes in the public interest; Art 5(1)(b) scientific research purposes; Art 5(1)(b) historical research purposes; Art 5(1)(b) statistical purposes; Art 5(1)(b) some other purpose.
      `the processing is necessary for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the processing is necessary for that purpose? Answer true or false.
      `the processing is in accordance with Article 89(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the processing is in accordance with Article 89(1)? Answer true or false.
      `it is based on Union or Member State law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that it is based on Union or Member State law? Answer true or false.
      `that law is proportionate to the aim pursued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that that law is proportionate to the aim pursued? Answer true or false.
      `that law respects the essence of the right to data protection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that that law respects the essence of the right to data protection? Answer true or false.
      `that law provides for suitable and specific measures to safeguard the fundamental rights and the interests of the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that that law provides for suitable and specific measures to safeguard the fundamental rights and the interests of the data subject? Answer true or false.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 9(2)(j), as a controller, does point (j) (archiving, research or statistical purposes) apply to my processing` IS
    `Art 9(2)(j) point (j) applies: the processing is necessary for archiving, research or statistical purposes in accordance with Article 89(1)` `the purpose` `the processing is necessary for that purpose` `the processing is in accordance with Article 89(1)` `it is based on Union or Member State law` `that law is proportionate to the aim pursued` `that law respects the essence of the right to data protection` `that law provides for suitable and specific measures to safeguard the fundamental rights and the interests of the data subject`

@export Under Article 9(2), as a controller, does one of points (a) to (j) apply to my processing?
GIVEN `point (a) applies: explicit consent` IS A `P1 controller answer` @desc Does point (a) (explicit consent) apply to your processing? Answer P1 controller answer: yes, P1 controller answer: no or P1 controller answer: not sure (not sure is treated as not covered).
      `point (b) applies: employment and social security and social protection law` IS A `P1 controller answer` @desc Does point (b) (employment and social security and social protection law) apply to your processing? Answer P1 controller answer: yes, P1 controller answer: no or P1 controller answer: not sure (not sure is treated as not covered).
      `point (c) applies: vital interests where the data subject cannot give consent` IS A `P1 controller answer` @desc Does point (c) (vital interests where the data subject cannot give consent) apply to your processing? Answer P1 controller answer: yes, P1 controller answer: no or P1 controller answer: not sure (not sure is treated as not covered).
      `point (d) applies: a not-for-profit body and its members` IS A `P1 controller answer` @desc Does point (d) (a not-for-profit body and its members) apply to your processing? Answer P1 controller answer: yes, P1 controller answer: no or P1 controller answer: not sure (not sure is treated as not covered).
      `point (e) applies: data manifestly made public by the data subject` IS A `P1 controller answer` @desc Does point (e) (data manifestly made public by the data subject) apply to your processing? Answer P1 controller answer: yes, P1 controller answer: no or P1 controller answer: not sure (not sure is treated as not covered).
      `point (f) applies: legal claims or courts acting in their judicial capacity` IS A `P1 controller answer` @desc Does point (f) (legal claims or courts acting in their judicial capacity) apply to your processing? Answer P1 controller answer: yes, P1 controller answer: no or P1 controller answer: not sure (not sure is treated as not covered).
      `point (g) applies: substantial public interest` IS A `P1 controller answer` @desc Does point (g) (substantial public interest) apply to your processing? Answer P1 controller answer: yes, P1 controller answer: no or P1 controller answer: not sure (not sure is treated as not covered).
      `point (h) applies: health or social care` IS A `P1 controller answer` @desc Does point (h) (health or social care) apply to your processing? Answer P1 controller answer: yes, P1 controller answer: no or P1 controller answer: not sure (not sure is treated as not covered).
      `point (i) applies: public interest in the area of public health` IS A `P1 controller answer` @desc Does point (i) (public interest in the area of public health) apply to your processing? Answer P1 controller answer: yes, P1 controller answer: no or P1 controller answer: not sure (not sure is treated as not covered).
      `point (j) applies: archiving, research or statistical purposes` IS A `P1 controller answer` @desc Does point (j) (archiving, research or statistical purposes) apply to your processing? Answer P1 controller answer: yes, P1 controller answer: no or P1 controller answer: not sure (not sure is treated as not covered).
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 9(2), as a controller, does one of points (a) to (j) apply to my processing` IS
    `Art 9(2) one of points (a) to (j) applies` (`P1 controller answer as a yes or no` `point (a) applies: explicit consent`) (`P1 controller answer as a yes or no` `point (b) applies: employment and social security and social protection law`) (`P1 controller answer as a yes or no` `point (c) applies: vital interests where the data subject cannot give consent`) (`P1 controller answer as a yes or no` `point (d) applies: a not-for-profit body and its members`) (`P1 controller answer as a yes or no` `point (e) applies: data manifestly made public by the data subject`) (`P1 controller answer as a yes or no` `point (f) applies: legal claims or courts acting in their judicial capacity`) (`P1 controller answer as a yes or no` `point (g) applies: substantial public interest`) (`P1 controller answer as a yes or no` `point (h) applies: health or social care`) (`P1 controller answer as a yes or no` `point (i) applies: public interest in the area of public health`) (`P1 controller answer as a yes or no` `point (j) applies: archiving, research or statistical purposes`)

@export Under Article 9(1) and (2), as a controller, is my processing of this category of personal data prohibited?
GIVEN `the category of the personal data` IS A `Art 9(1) category of personal data` @desc The category of the personal data: choose exactly one of: Art 9(1) data revealing racial or ethnic origin; Art 9(1) data revealing political opinions; Art 9(1) data revealing religious or philosophical beliefs; Art 9(1) data revealing trade union membership; Art 9(1) genetic data; Art 9(1) biometric data for the purpose of uniquely identifying a natural person; Art 9(1) data concerning health; Art 9(1) data concerning a natural person's sex life or sexual orientation; Art 9(1) biometric data not for the purpose of uniquely identifying a natural person; Art 9(1) other personal data.
      `one of points (a) to (j) of Article 9(2) applies` IS A `P1 controller answer` @desc Does one of the ten points of Article 9(2) apply to the processing (for example explicit consent, or data manifestly made public)? Answer P1 controller answer: yes, P1 controller answer: no or P1 controller answer: not sure (not sure is treated as not covered).
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 9(1) and (2), as a controller, is my processing of this category of personal data prohibited` IS
    `Art 9(1) the processing of personal data of a category named in paragraph 1 is prohibited` (LIST `the category of the personal data`) (`P1 controller answer as a yes or no` `one of points (a) to (j) of Article 9(2) applies`)

@export Under Article 9(3), as a controller, may personal data referred to in paragraph 1 be processed for the purposes of point (h) of paragraph 2?
GIVEN `the processing is for the purposes referred to in point (h) of paragraph 2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case, for your processing, that the processing is for the purposes referred to in point (h) of paragraph 2? Answer true or false.
