    `Art 9(3) personal data referred to in paragraph 1 may be processed for the purposes referred to in point (h) of paragraph 2` `the processing is for the purposes referred to in point (h) of paragraph 2` `the data are processed by or under the responsibility of a professional subject to the obligation of professional secrecy under Union or Member State law or rules established by national competent bodies` `the data are processed by another person also subject to an obligation of secrecy under Union or Member State law or rules established by national competent bodies`

@export Under Article 9(4), as a controller, may a Member State maintain or introduce further conditions for this category of personal data?
